/** \page requirements Requirements

@section GeneralRequirements General Requirements

The Platinum C++ framework can be compiled for any platform, which provides
an ISO C++ implementation. Exception support is a strong requirement, i.e.
it is and will never be possible to compile the framework without support
for exceptions. At the moment, RTTI is required, but might be optional in
the future. Usage of the C++ standard library (STL, IOStreams...) is limited
to a subset that works across many platforms. If you encounter a problem here
we would like to hear from you and solve it.

The system dependent parts of %Pt, such as the systems programming module, 
are designed to be very portable. The build process supports a variety
of platforms and compilers. See the "Supported Platforms" page for more
information.

It is useful to install subversion on the build host to get the source code
directly from the repository.

@section Unix Linux and Unix

In order to compile %Pt, you need to install the gnu toolchain, i.e. the
gnu C and C++ compiler, the linker and binutils. The UI module requires 
X11 headers and libraries to be installed. If possible, install also the
freetype headers and libraries, as Xft often depends on that.

@section Windows Windows

Install one of the Visual Studio versions mentioned on the "Supported 
Platforms" page. An express version will also work. Only the Windows UI
library is required to build the UI module.

@section OSX Mac OS-X

Install the Xcode developer tools to get a C and C++ and the other required
tools, headers and libraries. The UI module uses the CoreFoundation and 
cocoa frameworks. The system and networking modules requires the posix APIs.

@section WindowsCE Windows CE

Only Visual Studio 2005 and 2008 have support for Windows CE and Windows Mobile.
Older toolsets are not supported. Only the Windows UI library is required to 
build the UI module.

@section QNX QNX

The QNX developer tools must be installed. Cross compiling on a windows host, 
is supported as well as compiling directly on a QNX system. Only QNX Neutrino
is supported. To build the UI library Photon is required which normally comes
with the developer tools.

*/
